WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.810
So now all of a sudden in the wake of the
Trump Ukraine whistleblower Biden scandal,

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:11.500
as we are sort of calling it democratic speaker
of the house, Nancy Pelosi is considering

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.830
impeaching Donald Trump.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.630
There's a Washington post report, very detailed
that, uh, Nancy Pelosi up until last night

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.820
on the phone quietly sort of feeling out house
Democrats about whether to start an impeachment

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.940
inquiry as a result of this.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.560
Most recent scandal involving Donald Trump
and Ukraine and Joe bide.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.940
Now, to remind you my position on this, my
position on on impeachment has been a sort

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.300
of a, a neutral in the sense that I'm fine
doing it.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.370
I'm fine not doing it, but a decision has
to be made and whether there is or isn't going

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:48.610
to be an impeachment inquiry, Democrats need
to move forward on how to win in 2020 regardless

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.200
of what the impeachment decision is.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.490
Either use the impeachment inquiry to try
to win in 2020 or say we're not doing the

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.020
impeachment inquiry and figure out how to
win in 2020 anyway.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:04.239
Now, according to multiple senior house Democrats
and congressional AIDS, Nancy Pelosi is asking

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:10.310
around, is this Ukraine thing, the tipping
point, making phone calls all day yesterday

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.049
up to last night.

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:16.599
And there's a key line from this Washington
post report about this story, which is that

00:01:16.599 --> 00:01:22.509
there are now many leadership AIDS who once
thought Donald Trump's impeachment was unlikely

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:26.560
who are now saying they believe it to be almost
inevitable.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.909
Remember that Nancy Pelosi's previous position
was, Oh, impeachment will be too divisive.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:36.849
So the question is what has changed and what
has changed is the Ukraine story, which pulls

00:01:36.849 --> 00:01:44.109
together collusion, bribery, geopolitical
extortion, suppression of whistleblowers,

00:01:44.109 --> 00:01:50.789
and this is extending interest in impeachment
reportedly beyond just like the liberal base

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:56.020
of house Democrats to more centrist Democrats
as well.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.809
Democrats are admitting that the sort of tone
and tenor of conversations around impeachment

00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:06.840
have changed since the Ukraine story broke,
and although nothing has been finalized, it's

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.930
important to remember that even if an MP impeachment
inquiry did start, it could take some time,

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.030
which I don't think is bad.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:18.269
I've said before, the decision about the impeachment
inquiry should be made.

00:02:18.269 --> 00:02:24.040
The timing of it might be calculated to be
more damaging to Trump if it's delayed a little

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.549
bit until you know, maybe early 2020 would
be the latest that I think it would make sense

00:02:28.549 --> 00:02:29.730
to start it.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:35.680
But then you also see Democrats wasting time
with certain things around the Ukraine story.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.260
Here's an example.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:44.510
House Democrats are now planning to hold a
vote on a resolution to maybe condemn Donald

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.500
Trump's actions in regard to this Ukraine
Joe Biden thing.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.599
It's just a milk toast, irrelevant thing.

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:51.950
I mean, truly, I get it.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:56.740
You know, you get something on the record,
but the, this, this, it's just a waste.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.629
You're not gonna do anything with that.

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:05.439
And the idea of Ukraine as the tipping point,
if international extortion of other countries

00:03:05.439 --> 00:03:11.959
for the benefit of Donald Trump's 2020 election
chances by getting Ukraine to smear Biden

00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:13.970
is not a tipping point.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.469
Something is very wrong.

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:19.280
But we already had many of what should have
been tipping points in the past already.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.700
The firing of the FBI director James Comey,
Donald Trump's eight obstructive acts, Donald

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.879
Trump's supporting the Saudi war on Yemen,
the financial crimes and coverups, I mean

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:32.359
to say we are now at a tipping point is accurate.

00:03:32.359 --> 00:03:35.810
But it also ignores that we've had a number
of tipping points already.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:41.970
So what we get to in the end is that Nancy
Pelosi now reconsidering impeachment, it's

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.030
just the political calculation.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.380
Don't be tricked into thinking that what Nancy
Pelosi is calculating is whether what Donald

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:55.109
Trump has done is bad enough to justify an
impeachment inquiry or impeachment proceedings.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:04:00.980
They want us to think that they're evaluating
whether what Trump did is bad enough to justify

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:01.980
impeachment.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.549
What they're really doing and what Nancy Pelosi
is doing is calculating whether politically

00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:10.389
impeachment is likely to be a successful move.

00:04:10.389 --> 00:04:16.430
And when I say successful, I don't mean removing
Trump before the November, 2020 election with

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.639
Republicans controlling the Senate.

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:22.019
You're not going to remove Donald Trump through
impeachment.

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:26.949
The question is, would impeachment be successful
in the sense of being welcomed as the correct

00:04:26.949 --> 00:04:28.930
move by the public?

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.680
Would it be potentially beneficial for the
2020 election?

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.590
That is what Nancy Pelosi is now considering
and I want to hear from you.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.590
What do you think?

